<%#
  Icon safe areas — read before regenerating any of these PNGs.

  A `maskable` icon is cropped by the launcher to its own shape (circle,
  squircle, teardrop…). Per the W3C spec only the centred circle of diameter
  80% of the icon is guaranteed to survive. One file may serve both purposes
  (an icon can declare `"any maskable"`), but only if its artwork already sits
  inside that circle — a full-bleed image cannot. Ours is full-bleed at the
  `any` size, so maskable gets its own more-padded file; pointing both at the
  one full-bleed image is what clipped the wordmark's outer letters on Android.

  Current geometry (artwork is the Artifact crystal mark, from public/logo-offline.png):
    any / apple-touch  -> artwork at 72% of the canvas (~14% side margin)
    maskable           -> artwork at 59%, so its corners need a 79.6% circle
                          and clear the 80% safe zone

  iOS reads this file (manifest `icons` since 15.4), but the
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon"> tags in layouts/shared/_head.html.erb take
  precedence for the Home Screen icon, so in practice those are what ship.
  iOS reserves no safe area and composites transparency onto black, so they
  must stay opaque and self-padded.
%>
{
  "name": "<%= j product_name %>",
  "short_name": "<%= j product_name %>",
  "icons": [
    {
      "src": "<%= private_asset_path("android-chrome-192x192.png", v: ArtifinancePresentation.asset_version) %>",
      "type": "image/png",
      "sizes": "192x192"
    },
    {
      "src": "<%= private_asset_path("logo-pwa.png", v: ArtifinancePresentation.asset_version) %>",
      "type": "image/png",
      "sizes": "512x512"
    },
    {
      "src": "<%= private_asset_path("logo-pwa-maskable.png", v: ArtifinancePresentation.asset_version) %>",
      "type": "image/png",
      "sizes": "512x512",
      "purpose": "maskable"
    }
  ],
  "start_url": "/",
  "display": "standalone",
  "display_override": ["window-controls-overlay", "minimal-ui"],
  "scope": "/",
  "orientation": "any",
  "description": "<%= j product_name %> keeps all your money in one place.",
  "theme_color": "#F9F9F9",
  "background_color": "#F9F9F9"
}
